# Template. Copy to  supabase/.env  (which is git-ignored) and edit that copy.
# The Supabase CLI auto-loads supabase/.env and substitutes these values into
# the env(...) refs in config.toml (the [auth.email.smtp] block).
#
# Email in this app is sent by Supabase Auth over SMTP — the confirmation and
# password-reset links. There is no place in the app code that sends email,
# and an API key must never go in the browser bundle, so a provider is wired
# in here as an SMTP relay, not as an SDK call.

# ============================================================================
# CHOSEN PROVIDER: Resend  (https://resend.com)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free tier: 3,000 emails/month, 100/day. No card needed to sign up. Best
# deliverability of the free options.
#
#   Get the key: Resend dashboard -> API Keys -> Create API Key (starts re_).
#
# !!! DOMAIN CATCH: until you verify a sending DOMAIN in Resend, it only
#     delivers to the address the Resend account signed up with
#     (arcooreacc@gmail.com). Every other recipient gets a 403 and their
#     signup fails - fine for testing your own account, NOT usable for real
#     users. To fix, before a real beta:
#       Resend dashboard -> Domains -> Add Domain -> add the DNS records it
#       shows -> wait for "Verified" -> change SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL below to an
#       address at that domain (e.g. noreply@yourdomain.com).
#     Until then, the Brevo fallback lower down HAS no domain requirement.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.resend.com
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=resend
SMTP_PASS=                                  # <<< paste your re_ key here
SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev      # change to noreply@yourdomain.com once a domain is verified

# ============================================================================
# FALLBACK: Brevo  (https://www.brevo.com)   — no domain needed
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free: 300/day (9,000/month). Sends to ANY recipient with just a verified
# sender address, no domain. Deliverability a notch below Resend. Swap this
# block in (and comment out Resend above) if you need working email before a
# Resend domain is verified.
#
#   1. Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs -> Senders -> add arcooreacc@gmail.com,
#      click the verify link Brevo emails you.
#   2. SMTP & API -> SMTP tab: copy the "Login", generate an SMTP key.
#
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
#   SMTP_PORT=587
#   SMTP_USER=<the Login from step 2>
#   SMTP_PASS=<the xsmtpsib-... key from step 2>
#   SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=arcooreacc@gmail.com

# ============================================================================
# LOCAL-ONLY: Mailpit test inbox (http://127.0.0.1:54324)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captures every message, never delivers. Swap in for offline local testing;
# the demo seed accounts (demo-*@test.local / demopass123) are pre-confirmed
# so signup email isn't needed to test the app locally.
#
#   SMTP_HOST=inbucket
#   SMTP_PORT=1025
#   SMTP_USER=mailpit
#   SMTP_PASS=mailpit
#   SMTP_ADMIN_EMAIL=arcooreacc@gmail.com

# After editing supabase/.env:
#   ./.tools/supabase.exe stop && ./.tools/supabase.exe start
# To carry it to the hosted project (part of a full deploy):
#   ./.tools/supabase.exe config push

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (bot protection on login + signup) --------------
# Free at https://dash.cloudflare.com -> Turnstile. Put the Site Key in
# public/js/env.js (not secret - it ships in the page); put the Secret Key
# here, then set [auth.captcha] enabled = true in supabase/config.toml.
TURNSTILE_SECRET=

# ============================================================================
# Social sign-in — Google / Microsoft
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# env.js already lists 'google' + 'azure' in SITESTOCK_OAUTH_PROVIDERS. All
# that's left per provider: register an OAuth app with it, paste its two
# values below, set [auth.external.<provider>] enabled = true in config.toml,
# then restart (or `config push` for hosted).
#
# Full click-by-click, including the exact redirect URLs for local + hosted:
#   supabase/OAUTH_SETUP.md
#
# Apple is intentionally NOT set up - it needs the $99/yr Apple Developer
# Program; deferred until SiteStock is wrapped as a native app (Snagging List).
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_SECRET=
AZURE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
AZURE_OAUTH_SECRET=
